        "text": "Then coins and paper money were created to represent a fixed amount of a physical commodity like gold in a system called the gold standard. The gold standard solved the problem of portability and divisibility for bricks of gold. Today, coins and paper notes only account for a small fraction of the monetary system. Most of the money in the world is digital money, recorded in the ledgers of banks and other financial institutions. No economy uses the gold standard anymore, although most countries do keep some gold reserves. That's where fiat money comes in.",
